BadChar: bad URL "http://a b": a URL holds no space or control character; write a space as `%20` (at 8)
BadEscape: bad URL "http://x/%zz": `%` starts an escape of two hexadecimal digits; write `%` itself as `%25` (at 9)
BadScheme: bad URL "1a:b": a scheme starts with a letter and holds only letters, digits, `+`, `-` and `.` (at 2)
BadPort: bad URL "http://h:99999": a port is at most 65535 (at 9)
BadPort: bad URL "http://h:8x": a port is digits (at 10)
BadHost: bad URL "http://[::1": an IPv6 address needs its closing `]` (at 7)
BadHost: bad URL "http://[zz]": `[...]` holds an IPv6 address: hexadecimal digits, `:` and `.` (at 8)
